    {
      "label": "H2: Systematic timing‑device calibration error",
      "probability": 0.10,
      "rationale": "If the same stopwatch or timing circuit was recalibrated or drifted after day 10, both pendulum measurements would inherit a common offset, while resonator calculations (which use an independent frequency counter) would be unaffected.",
      "evidenceFor": ["513526","243406","5489","896437","591357","812189","985476","1028383","727233","797104","17182","943207","725088"],
      "evidenceAgainst": ["no documented change to the timing hardware", "the magnitude of drift is similar in both pendulums despite different swing amplitudes"]
